course: dictionary
lesson: 4032
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning over time, and people use them differently in different places. «Gay» is one of these words. In old books it meant merry and bright, and in everyday life today it usually describes a person who is romantically attracted to people of the same sex.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. «Toad sang gay songs as he rode along the lane.» Toad is happy and full of fun, so gay means merry and cheerful. Always ask: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: Some people use «gay» as an insult to mean «bad» or «stupid». This is hurtful and wrong, so never use it that way. Using words with respect for other people is part of reading and writing well.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Gay» (old-fashioned) means happy, merry and full of fun, as in «gay songs».
fact: «Gay» (old-fashioned) can also mean bright and colourful, as in «the river was gay with flowers».
fact: Today «gay» usually describes a person who is romantically attracted to people of the same sex. Gay people should be treated with respect.
fact: Alan Turing was gay. The law in Britain at the time made this a crime, and the government apologised in 2009. Today he is on the £50 note.
exercise: Toad sang «gay songs» as he rode along the lane. What does gay mean here? | Dirty and wet | Loud and rude | *Merry and cheerful | Sad and slow
exercise: «The river was gay with flowers.» Which word could you swap in for gay? | Silent | Empty | Frozen | *Bright
exercise: Why should we use the word gay with respect? | Because it is an old word for stupid | Because it only means happy | Because it means bad | *Because gay people deserve respect, like everyone else
test: Someone says «that's so gay» to mean rubbish. What is wrong with this? | *It is a hurtful insult, and it is bullying language | Nothing, it is a fun slang word | It is a perfect way to describe a rainy day | It is an old word for happy
test: Which sentence uses gay in its old meaning? | Gay people should be treated with respect | *Toad appeared fresh and gay, remarking what a pleasant easy life it was | Some families have two dads or two mums | Alan Turing was gay and was pardoned in 2013
exam: Which statement is true? | Gay is always an insult and should never be used | Gay only ever meant happy, and it has never changed | *Gay has an old meaning of merry and bright, and a modern meaning about people attracted to people of the same sex | Gay means the same as sad in every book
